<title>INDIA: Motorola, Ericsson to build India Reliance network.</title>
<headline>Motorola, Ericsson to build India Reliance network.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. firm Motorola and Sweden's Ericsson have been selected by India's Reliance Telecom to build a system for a mobile telephone communications, the Indian firm said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>&quot;The decision to entrust this key contract followed international competitive bids and their track record in building cellular systems,&quot; the firm said in a statement.</p>
<p>Reliance Telecom is promoted by giant petrochemicals firm Reliance Industries Ltd.</p>
<p>The company has been licensed to provide cellular services to 13 Indian states which have a combined population of over 300 million people, it said.</p>
<p>--Bombay Newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
